course: dictionary
lesson: 9040
title: Slavery: a word with a heavy meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Slavery is a serious word. It names a cruel system in which people are owned by other people, forced to work for no pay and have no freedom. The context shows this: «Ethan's friend says slavery ended in 1865, done.» The word ended tells you slavery is something that can stop, and done tells you his friend thinks the job is finished.
explain: Context can also show that a simple sentence may hide more. «On 4 July 1776 they declared independence, saying all men are created equal, though slavery went on» shows that people who wrote fine words about freedom still kept slavery. The word though is a clue that something does not fit.
explain: Read the next clue with care: «Brazil ... in 1888 it was the last country in the Americas to abolish slavery.» Last means final, and abolish means to end something by law. When a word is heavy like this, use the clues to understand it, then check a dictionary to be sure.
fact: Slavery means a cruel system in which people are owned by other people, forced to work for no pay and have no freedom.
fact: Slavery can also mean the state of being a slave, or very hard work or control that feels like being owned, as in «modern slavery».
fact: The people who fought to end slavery were called abolitionists, such as William Wilberforce, Frederick Douglass and Harriet Tubman.
fact: Britain banned its slave trade in 1807 and slavery in most of its colonies from 1834, while slavery lasted in the USA until 1865 and in Brazil until 1888.
fact: Slavery is a clear example of a great wrong, and people today still speak of «modern slavery» when people are forced to work.
exercise: «Ethan's friend says slavery ended in 1865, done.» What does done suggest about his friend? | He is hungry | He is sad about slavery | *He thinks the matter is finished | He is counting the days
exercise: «Brazil ... was the last country in the Americas to abolish slavery.» What does last tell you? | It was the happiest country there | It was the biggest country in the Americas | It was the first country to start slavery | *It was the final country there to end slavery
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Ordinary people ... signed petitions until slavery was banned» that means made illegal by law. | sweets | *banned | petitions | helped
test: Slavery means a system where people are what? | Free to move house | *Owned by other people | Paid well for their work | Given a fair wage
test: Which word means to end something by law? | *Abolish | Wages | Owner | Harvest
exam: Which sentence uses slavery correctly? | Slavery is a kind of sweets | Ethan said the bus was slavery | We ate slavery for lunch | *The abolition of slavery was a great step towards freedom
